"""RHEL OS-only, three-phase, same-account EC2 upgrade performance reporting.

Python 3.12/3.13 AWS Lambda. Dependency: boto3 (included in AWS Lambda Python runtime).
Outputs four user-facing HTML reports (phase-1.html, phase-2.html, phase-3.html,
final-summary.html). Every phase also publishes phase-N-status.json in the batch
folder and .state/phase-N.json (historical data used in the final comparison).
Uses EXACT renamed metric names from the supplied CWAgent configuration.

Required Lambda environment variables:
  REPORT_BUCKET, REPORT_PREFIX, KMS_KEY_ARN
Optional:
  CW_AGENT_NAMESPACE=CWAgent
  SSM_WAIT_SECONDS=100
  BASELINE_DAYS=15
  MAX_HOSTS=20
  MAX_DISCOVERED_SERVICES=80

Run 1 Test event:
{
 "phase": 1, "batch_id": "nov26-wave01",
 "hostnames": ["APP-SERVER-01", "DB-SERVER-01"],
 "server_types": {"APP-SERVER-01":"app", "DB-SERVER-01":"db"},
 "service_exclusions_by_host": {"APP-SERVER-01": ["custom-one-off.service"]}
}
Run 2 / Run 3 Test event:
{
 "phase": 2, "batch_id": "nov26-wave01",
 "upgrade_completed_at_utc": {
   "APP-SERVER-01":"2026-11-20T03:30:00Z",
   "DB-SERVER-01":"2026-11-21T05:15:00Z"
 }
}
For Run 3 change phase to 3, and supply the second upgrade completion times.
No automatic upgrade-time guess: last reboot is not a reliable upgrade timestamp.
Non-core systemd services (custom/vendor/monitoring/application service units)
are auto-discovered in Phase 1 and compared after upgrades. Discovery filters
common RHEL OS services by name; the classification is best-effort and can be
refined with service_exclusions_by_host at Phase 1.

Important: CWAgent must have collected historical memory/disk/swap metrics in advance.
SSM OS snapshots capture the state AT EACH RUN, not a 15-day retrospective.
"""

